    "rarity": "rare",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>This large revolver has some heft to it, making you realize that what you see outside of the gun is only a small percentage of the technology packed into this firearm. The long barrel feels perfectly balanced once the user has it in a firing position, granting the user unparalleled comfort while firing. The handle of the gun is made up of a material that carefully forms around the hands of the user.</p>\n<h3>Properties</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Attack:</strong> +1 to hit (DEX-based ranged weapon)</li>\n<li><strong>Damage:</strong> 2d6 + DEX modifier force damage</li>\n<li><strong>Ergonomic Grip:</strong> Disarming attacks are made with disadvantage against the wielder of this weapon</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Overload</h3>\n<p><img src=\"modules/elysium/assets/icons/ElysiumDefenderOverload.png\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;\"><strong>Overload:</strong> As an action, you can push the weapon beyond its limits, channeling raw aether through its core. The damage doubles to <strong>4d6 + DEX modifier</strong> force damage for that attack.</p>\n<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Consumes 1 aether fuel charge. You gain 1 daily dose and 1 Aether Toxicity Level.</p>\n<p><strong>Risk:</strong> After the overloaded shot, roll a d20. If the result is equal to or less than <strong>2 + (ATL &times; 2)</strong>, the weapon's internal mechanisms seize up and it becomes inert until you complete a long rest.</p>\n<p class=\"elysium-info-box\"><strong>Warning:</strong> Overloading becomes increasingly dangerous as Aether Toxicity accumulates. At ATL 0 you fail on a 1-2, at ATL 1 on a 1-4, at ATL 2 on a 1-6, and so on.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
